# Windows mutex prerequisite summary

Implemented the standalone cross-session mutex primitive and platform-neutral acceptance policy. The native adapter uses `windows-sys 0.61.2`, an effective-token SID, explicit protected owner/DACL security, post-open descriptor inspection, a bounded wait, sanitized failures, and a thread-bound RAII guard.

Checks passed:

- Linux all-target suite: 117 passed.
- Formatting check, Clippy with `-D warnings`, release build: passed.
- Isolated `x86_64-pc-windows-msvc` `cargo check --all-targets`: passed against the real module and bindings.
- Test-first evidence includes an executable red failure followed by the passing suite; details and source links are in `windows-lock-evidence.md`.

Windows runtime tests (acquire/drop, contention, incompatible descriptor, abandoned owner) are **PENDING**; no Windows binary was run. The isolated check does not establish whole-CLI Windows compatibility. Work stopped before credential storage/backend/browser changes.

